

1) --> What is XML-based Configuration in Spring?

XML-based configuration means:
    We define beans
    Their dependencies
    Their lifecycle
    Their scope
👉 inside an XML file, instead of writing configuration in Java code or annotations.
📌 Spring reads this XML file and creates + manages objects for us.



2) --> Why XML Configuration Was Used Before Annotations?

Before Spring 2.5:
     Java annotations did not exist
     No @Component, @Autowired, @Configuration

So developers used:
    XML files for object creation
    XML for dependency injection
    XML for lifecycle control

Advantages at that time:
    No modification needed in Java classes
    Configuration separated from business logic
    Easy to change behavior without recompiling code